MUST-FIX

1. Missing AC annotations on the three newly added plan-import tests in "'`tests/cli-plan-import.test.ts` (around lines 1050, 1090, 1129).

The repo relies on `// AC: @spec-ref ac-N` annotations for AC coverage accounting. These new tests exercise `@plan-import` behavior (including dry-run output), but none of them are annotated, so coverage tooling cannot attribute them.

Suggested fix:
- Add `// AC: @plan-import ...` comments above each new test.
- If the root-trait placement behavior is not represented by an existing `@plan-import` AC, add/update the spec AC first, then annotate the tests accordingly.
- The dry-run test should be annotated to `@plan-import ac-15`.

SHOULD-FIX

1. The linked task (`@01KJ4SM6`) does not have a formal `spec_ref`; I inferred `@plan-import` from the task notes. This makes automated AC review less reliable.

What I checked

- `gh pr diff 480`
- `gh pr view 480 --json title,body,files`
- `kspec task get @01KJ4SM6` and `--json`
- `kspec item get @plan-import` and `--json` (no inherited traits)
- `pnpm vitest tests/cli-plan-import.test.ts --run` (passes)
- `kspec validate` (fails on existing repo-wide reference/alignment/completeness issues; no `@plan-import` or trait-AC-specific warnings surfaced for this PR)

Code review notes

- The root trait write path in `src/cli/commands/plan-import.ts` matches the existing manifest-write logic used by `kspec trait add`, so the behavior change itself looks correct.
- The new tests cover the intended placement behavior (root trait to `kynetic.yaml`, child trait stays under parent, dry-run messaging) but need AC annotations.
